# Reference material for checking architectural claims, fetched by
# scripts/fetch-references.sh. Large and redistributable only from Intel.
.references/

# Agent worktrees and scratch state. Never part of the tree.
.claude/worktrees/
scratchpad/

# Recorded by scripts/deploy-to-rig.sh so a confusing boot can be checked
# against what was actually deployed. Per-machine, not per-tree.
# Everything deploy-to-rig.sh leaves behind, as a pattern rather than a
# list. The list was the bug: it named the hash and the ELF, missed the
# loader, and a 2 MB binary was then committed and re-committed with new
# contents on every deploy. A prefix cannot miss the next one.
.rig-deployed*

# Python leaves these beside any script imported as a module.
__pycache__/

# The decoder harness writes its corpus beside itself, assembles it with
# llvm-mc and reads the listing back. Outputs of a run, not inputs to
# one - the corpus is generated by the harness, which is why nothing
# lists it.
tests/decoder/corpus-*.s
tests/decoder/corpus-*.dis
